{"event_type":"review","id":"33923dcb97f7227f535bebc744a1fc9e29a13402c1e66c8dc98b9bf94f962529","occurred_at":"2026-11-16T22:57:28Z","payload":{"artifacts":[{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/39dda7073d627ec285d47a7ddfed48816e944946e3084c842479e655e29c34f3","sha256":"39dda7073d627ec285d47a7ddfed48816e944946e3084c842479e655e29c34f3"},{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/1ec313e8e3452430096adf955b91f4d65adac5f1aa70990d8f58146f4091b512","sha256":"1ec313e8e3452430096adf955b91f4d65adac5f1aa70990d8f58146f4091b512"},{"kind":"git-bundle","location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/6f23ace339fbc90a440f1846bfe720410e0ff69a66c6ff68c3077650751c1569","sha256":"6f23ace339fbc90a440f1846bfe720410e0ff69a66c6ff68c3077650751c1569"},{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/0273ac1aab3760522688f8de98f1e8b5df94192023a89be57bf1f273711927ff","sha256":"0273ac1aab3760522688f8de98f1e8b5df94192023a89be57bf1f273711927ff"},{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/3798cc1548b0a47586c73c88cc26a8f75c903605e75fdfd9107caf4e83d00e03","sha256":"3798cc1548b0a47586c73c88cc26a8f75c903605e75fdfd9107caf4e83d00e03"}],"attempt_id":"44de758be3a0cbce0b72f5490b6bcff1d1078770de6a984cbf6ec79eafc11eb3:0:1","base":"aafdceee72d6430c32789b4200bec6cba9baf9a3","completion":{"errors":[],"exit_code":0,"scope_verified":true,"skipped":false,"terminal":true},"findings":[{"anchor_status":"verified","blob":"50ddb1e1c85b8c77ab462a33c6a0196127ca2445","body":"**Use the same evidence snapshot for every check.**\n\nIn `src/ops/review/internal/addressVerification.ts`, coherence reads packet fields directly, and trigger checking reads them again. An `after` getter can return the actual snapshot during completeness and coherence, then return different content during trigger checking.\n\nFor example, supply a patch that replaces only the first of two `bad()` calls. If the later observation hides the second call, the verifier returns `resolved` although the validated patch retains that call. The dependency snapshot does not protect `after` or the other packet fields.\n\nCapture and validate the packet fields once. Use those captured values for every check and for the returned revision evidence.","id":"5a20ee9016a37c7bb09385d1393e98c32696cc36af86b8ac22423b73ac6bb722","intervals":[[448,448]],"path":"src/ops/review/internal/addressVerification.ts","severity":"major","source_id":null,"status":"untriaged","title":"Use the same evidence snapshot for every check."},{"anchor_status":"verified","blob":"50ddb1e1c85b8c77ab462a33c6a0196127ca2445","body":"**Do not equate trigger-text removal with a verified fix.**\n\nIn `src/ops/review/internal/addressVerification.ts`, this predicate accepts a textual rewrite that preserves the defect. For a finding that quotes `price - tax` and requires addition, change `const total = price - tax;` to `const total = (price) - tax;`. The quote disappears, `modifiedDeclaration` permits the replacement, and an otherwise complete packet returns `resolved`. The calculation still subtracts tax.\n\nKeep this case `uncertain` unless additional validated evidence establishes the required behavior. Text disappearance alone must not authorize closure.","id":"2cbddd02d6c7e8341666583bef466209aee01ff5564c749c1e60545f369dd6c9","intervals":[[561,565]],"path":"src/ops/review/internal/addressVerification.ts","severity":"major","source_id":null,"status":"untriaged","title":"Do not equate trigger-text removal with a verified fix."}],"head":"9528ca05c8efec4decdc7aeb15e0949ce56df1b2","head_tree":"2a6378f38614c8b16a7d30447cf71e2ddc2985f6","input_scope":[{"blob":"50ddb1e1c85b8c77ab462a33c6a0196127ca2445","intervals":[[1,631]],"path":"src/ops/review/internal/addressVerification.ts"}],"job_id":"44de758be3a0cbce0b72f5490b6bcff1d1078770de6a984cbf6ec79eafc11eb3:0","outcome":"completed","paths":[{"baseline":{"entry":null,"merge":"9611f57bb0175f83b2d138a0aac2